---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
const ja = Astro.props.lang === 'ja';
const proposal = 'https://github.com/matsumotory/ngx_mruby/blob/next/docs/proposals/edge-control.md';
// The proposal table owns status; the site only supplies explanatory copy.
const ledger = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), '../docs/proposals/edge-control.md'), 'utf8');
// Cells are split on unescaped pipes (GFM allows \| inside a cell), and the
// Status column is found by its header, not by its position.
const cells = line => line.split(/(?<!\\)\|/).slice(1, -1).map(cell => cell.trim());
const header = ledger.split('\n').find(line => /^\| Use case \|/.test(line));
const statusColumn = header ? cells(header).indexOf('Status') : -1;
if (statusColumn < 0) throw new Error('The use-case ledger has no Status column');
const states = new Map(ledger.split('\n').filter(line => /^\| \[.*\]\(#/.test(line)).map(line => {
  const fields = cells(line);
  const id = fields[0].match(/\]\(#([^)]*)\)/)?.[1];
  const status = fields[statusColumn]?.match(/`(designing|direction|next|2\.x)`/)?.[1];
  if (!id || !status) throw new Error('Invalid use-case ledger row');
  return [id, status];
}));
if (states.size !== ledger.split('\n').filter(line => /^\| \[.*\]\(#/.test(line)).length) {
  throw new Error('Duplicate use-case ledger id');
}
const cases = [
  { id: 'mcp-tool-authorization', status: 'designing',
    title: ['MCPツールの呼び出し権限を確認する', 'Check permissions for MCP tool calls'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "ユーザーごとにMCPツールと引数を制限する設計です。Rubyで認証済みユーザーの権限とtools/callの内容を照合し、許可した呼び出しをMCPサーバーへ転送します。",
        "個々のデータへのアクセス権限は、転送先のMCPサーバーでも検証する方針です。",
      ],
      [
        "An MCP service operator could restrict the tools and arguments available to each user. Ruby would compare tools/call with the authenticated user’s permissions and forward only allowed calls.",
        "The destination MCP server would still enforce access to individual data objects.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'mcp-burst-control', status: 'direction',
    title: ['MCP呼び出しの集中を制限する', 'Limit bursts of MCP calls'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "AIアプリケーションによる短時間の呼び出しや、多数のストリームで生じる負荷を制限する構想です。Rubyでユーザーと呼び出しの種類を識別し、nginxのlimit_reqとlimit_connで上限を適用します。",
        "必要な読み直しは許可します。制限を受けたアプリには、再試行できる条件を返す方針です。",
      ],
      [
        "To bound bursts of calls and open streams, Ruby would identify the user and call class. nginx limit_req and limit_conn would apply the configured limits.",
        "Legitimate rereads would still pass, and rejection responses would describe when the application can retry.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'mcp-tool-profiles', status: 'designing',
    title: ['AIアプリケーション別にMCPツールを出す', 'Fit the MCP tools to each AI application'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "異なるツール構成を必要とするAIアプリケーションから、同じMCPサービスを利用する設計です。接続プロファイルに応じて、MCPゲートウェイが転送先のMCPサーバーを選びます。",
        "ツールの一覧と呼び出し方の違いは、バージョンを付けた転送先で扱います。検索や取得の処理は、アプリ間で共用する方針です。",
      ],
      [
        "Different AI applications could use the same service through different MCP tool interfaces. The gateway would select a backend MCP server by connection profile.",
        "That versioned backend would provide consistent tools/list and tools/call behavior, without duplicating search and retrieval logic for each application.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'mcp-progressive-retrieval', status: 'designing',
    title: ['文書を必要な範囲から取得する', 'Retrieve the needed part of a document'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "エージェントが長い文書の必要な箇所をMCPツールで取得し、足りなければ読み足せるようにする設計です。MCPゲートウェイは取得方式と処理量の上限を選びます。",
        "文書の位置、バージョン、続きの取得はバックエンドが管理します。JSONやストリームを切り詰めず、範囲指定に対応する取得機能を使う構成を検討しています。",
      ],
      [
        "An agent could request the relevant passage of a long document, then read more if needed. The MCP gateway would select the retrieval profile and processing budget.",
        "The backend would manage positions, versions and continuation through a range-aware tool. The gateway would not truncate JSON or streams.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'mcp-next-step-guidance', status: 'direction',
    title: ['検索結果がない場合の次の手順を伝える', 'Return next steps when a search finds nothing'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "検索結果がない場合や取得に失敗した場合に、理由と次の手順をエージェントへ返す構想です。MCPゲートウェイは該当なし、権限不足、取得先の障害を区別して中継します。",
        "検索対象に固有の手掛かりはMCPサービスが提供します。文書中の指示を実行の指示として扱わず、検索を続けるか条件を変えるかはエージェントが判断する方針です。",
      ],
      [
        "When search or retrieval fails, an agent could receive the reason and available next steps. The gateway would preserve the distinction between no match, denied access and an unavailable source.",
        "The MCP service would supply domain-specific guidance. Retrieved instructions would not become execution instructions; the agent would decide whether to search again or change the query.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'mcp-trajectory-logging', status: 'direction',
    title: ['MCPツールの呼び出し順序を観測する', 'Observe sequences of MCP tool calls'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "MCPサービスの運用者が、検索、文書取得、再検索の順序と結果を調べる構想です。相関IDで呼び出しを関連付け、ツール名、成否、所要時間を記録します。",
        "検索語や文書本文は標準では収集せず、保存期間と収集量に上限を設けます。調査を続けるかはエージェントが判断します。",
      ],
      [
        "An MCP service operator could trace searches, document retrieval and repeated searches. A correlation ID would connect tool names, outcomes and durations.",
        "Queries and document bodies would not be collected by default. Retention and volume would be bounded, while the agent would decide whether to continue its investigation.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'llm-api-fallback', status: 'designing',
    title: ['モデルAPIのエラーで転送先を変える', 'Select another model API endpoint after an error'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "モデルAPIの切替をAIゲートウェイで管理する設計です。上流の429などの再送対象エラーに応じ、Rubyが互換性のある転送先と認証情報を選び、nginxが再送します。",
        "再送は安全に再実行できるリクエストに限り、回数と時間を制限します。応答を送り始めた後は、別の生成結果につなぎ替えない構成を検討しています。",
      ],
      [
        "An operator could manage model API fallback at the AI gateway. After an upstream 429 or another configured retryable error, Ruby would select a compatible endpoint and credentials for nginx to retry.",
        "Only requests safe to replay would be retried, with bounded attempts and time. A response already in progress would not be replaced by another generated stream.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'ai-crawler-and-bot-control', status: 'direction',
    title: ['AIクローラーとエージェントの頻度を絞る', 'Limit the request rate of AI crawlers and agents'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "WebサイトやAPIへのアクセス規則をRubyで選ぶ構想です。AIクローラーの巡回とユーザーの指示によるアクセスを区別し、頻度と同時接続数を制限します。",
        "User-Agentの自己申告だけを身元の証明とせず、署名などの検証方法と、識別できない相手の扱いを定める方針です。",
      ],
      [
        "A website or API operator could select policies for AI crawlers and agents. Ruby would distinguish collection by a crawler from access on a user’s behalf and choose rate and concurrency limits.",
        "A User-Agent claim would not prove identity. The design needs independent checks, such as request signatures, and a policy for unidentified clients.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'semantic-cache', status: 'direction',
    title: ['外部のセマンティックキャッシュを参照する', 'Consult an external semantic cache'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "似たリクエストに保存済みの回答を再利用し、アプリの処理を変えずにモデルAPIへの問い合わせを減らす構想です。AIゲートウェイがアクセス範囲やモデルの条件を渡し、外部サービスが再利用の可否を判断します。",
        "一致がない場合、判断が曖昧な場合、タイムアウト時は元のモデルAPIへ転送します。回答をキャッシュに保存する方式は未設計です。",
      ],
      [
        "An external semantic cache could reuse an answer for a similar request without changing the application. The gateway would supply the access scope and model; the cache service would decide whether reuse is valid.",
        "A miss, uncertain match or timeout would fall through to the original model API. Storage of responses in the cache is not yet designed.",
      ],
    ] },
  { id: 'log-handler-telemetry', status: 'direction',
    title: ['log handlerで記録した値を外部へ送る', 'Export metadata recorded by the log handler'],
    paragraphs: [
      [
        "サービスの運用者が、ステータス、応答時間、転送先を外部の集計基盤で確認する構想です。現在のlog handlerはネットワーク応答を待てないため、上限付きのワーカーキューとタイマーで送信する処理を計画しています。",
        "収集先の遅延で応答を止めないよう、ノンブロッキングな通信を使います。キューの満杯時や送信失敗時の扱いも定めます。",
      ],
      [
        "A service operator could send status, response times and routing decisions to an external collector. Since the current log handler cannot wait for a network response, export is planned through a bounded worker queue and timers.",
        "Non-blocking transport would keep collector delays from stalling responses. Behavior on a full queue or failed delivery would be defined.",
      ],
    ] },
];
// The copy of each case says 設計 or 構想 (design or direction), so a change
// of its row in the ledger stops the build until the copy is reviewed.
for (const item of cases) {
  if (states.get(item.id) !== item.status) throw new Error(`Review homepage use-case copy: ${item.id} is ${states.get(item.id)} in the ledger, ${item.status} in the copy`);
}
if (states.size !== cases.length) throw new Error('Homepage cases and proposal ledger differ');
const label = status => ja ? (status === 'designing' ? '設計中' : '構想') : (status === 'designing' ? 'Designing' : 'Direction');
---
<section class="v3-directions" aria-labelledby="directions-title">
  <div class="home-copy">
  <h2 id="directions-title">{ja ? '今後のユースケースと設計状況' : 'Future use cases and their design status'}</h2>
    {ja ? <>
      <p>モデル振り分けの実行例は手元で動かせます。以下は、MCPの認可、モデルAPIの切替、サイトへのアクセス制御に向けた設計です。次に何を検索し、どこを読み取るかをモデルが選ぶAIアプリケーションを、ここではエージェントと呼びます。</p>
      <p>「設計中」は実行例と検証条件を示し、「構想」は用途の方向性を示します。どちらも、用途全体を動かすテストはまだありません。必要な機能と制約の詳細は、各項目の設計文書で確認できます。</p>
    </> : <>
      <p>The model routing example above runs locally today. The following designs apply nginx and Ruby to MCP authorization, model API fallback and access to websites.</p>
      <p>An agent is an AI application whose model chooses the next search or read.</p>
      <p>“Designing” means the first recipe and acceptance criteria are documented. “Direction” means only the direction is documented.</p>
      <p>No test runs a complete use case in either status. Each design document lists the required features and constraints.</p>
    </>}
  </div>
  <div class="direction-list">
    {cases.map(item => <article class="direction-usecase" data-use-case={item.id}>
      <div class="direction-scan"><h3>{item.title[ja ? 0 : 1]}</h3><p class="direction-status"><span class="site-badge">{label(states.get(item.id))}</span></p></div>
      <div class="direction-body">{item.paragraphs[ja ? 0 : 1].map(text => <p>{text}</p>)}<a href={`${proposal}#${item.id}`}>{ja ? '設計と必要な機能を読む' : 'Read the design and required features'}</a></div>
    </article>)}
  </div>
</section>
